# Package directories use a whitelist: ignore everything, then allow recipes and
# local helper files back in.
#
# Not a blacklist, because downloaded file names are unpredictable — claude-code's
# binary is called claude-2.1.226-x86_64 with no extension at all, and no
# suffix-based rule catches it. That is how 565MB of binaries once ended up
# committed by `git add -A`. A whitelist has no such failure mode.
#
# If a package needs a new kind of local file tracked, add another ! line below.

/*/*
# The whitelist assumes "one top-level directory = one package", so non-package
# directories have to be allowed wholesale, or /*/* swallows things like
# .github/workflows (which it did, once).
!/.github/**
!/ci/**
!/tests/**
!/*/PKGBUILD
!/*/*.install
!/*/*.patch
!/*/*.hook
!/*/*.desktop
!/*/*.sh
!/*/*.c
!/*/*.html

# Top-level tooling is tracked as usual; only transient output is excluded.
nvchecker-new.json
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.log
